# weworking — secrets.
#
# The Deploy to Cloudflare button asks for every uncommented name in this file,
# so the optional ones are commented out. For `wrangler dev`, copy it to
# `.dev.vars` (git-ignored) and fill it in. For a deployed Worker set the same
# names with `npx wrangler secret put <NAME>` instead — never commit real values.
#
# Non-secret configuration (WRITE_ENABLED, MAX_BOOKINGS_PER_DAY,
# MAX_CREDITS_PER_BOOKING, MAX_CASH_PER_BOOKING, ...) lives in `wrangler.jsonc`
# under `vars`, not here. Both money caps default to "0": raise MAX_CASH_PER_BOOKING
# if your plan pays for desks in cash rather than in credits.

# --- WeWork member credentials (OPTIONAL) -----------------------------------
# Only needed if you want the Worker to log in by itself (LOGIN_STRATEGY=auto|headless).
# Auth0 frequently blocks datacenter IPs with `requires_verification`, and MFA is not
# supported, so the reliable path is: leave these empty, log in once in your own browser
# and paste the token at /admin/connect. See docs/SELF_HOSTING.md. Uncomment to use.
# WEWORK_USERNAME=""
# WEWORK_PASSWORD=""

# --- Admin access (REQUIRED) ------------------------------------------------
# Gates /admin/* (connect, API keys, audit log, status) and the OAuth approve screen.
# Use a long random passphrase.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=""

# --- API keys ---------------------------------------------------------------
# There is no secret for these. Sign in at /admin/keys and mint one; the worker
# stores its SHA-256 in the session Durable Object and shows you the key once.

# --- Signing keys (REQUIRED) ------------------------------------------------
# 32+ random bytes, hex. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint8Array(32)).reduce((s,b)=>s+b.toString(16).padStart(2,'0'),''))"
#
# Signs booking quotes (HMAC-SHA-256). create_booking only accepts a quote this key signed.
QUOTE_SIGNING_KEY=""
# Signs the /admin session cookie.
COOKIE_SIGNING_KEY=""
